{"id": "EUVD-2026-108711", "enisaUuid": "0ebdf962-dd37-3db8-a92e-2291f759b22d", "description": "Snap7 through 1.4.3 contains an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the passive partner that allows a malicious active partner to overflow application buffers by declaring an unvalidated BSend total length. Attackers connecting from the configured peer address can declare up to 65535 bytes and send a short fragment, causing BRecv to memcpy past the buffer and crash or corrupt SCADA, HMI or gateway processes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T11:36:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:36:47", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/davenardella/snap7/pull/41", "https://github.com/davenardella/snap7/blob/30f37da3114024a71ba93f7fd855c680b97a406f/src/core/s7_partner.cpp#L1126-L1166", "https://github.com/davenardella/snap7/blob/30f37da3114024a71ba93f7fd855c680b97a406f/src/core/s7_partner.cpp#L850-L867", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/snap7-through-1.4.3-out-of-bounds-write-via-brecv-and-checkasbrecvcompletion"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-115723"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c1716e2b-3190-3c0e-a441-3604d4499613", "product": {"name": "snap7", "vendor": {"name": "davenardella"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.4.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b03b3afb-9840-30be-bd8f-112c801324e4", "vendor": {"name": "davenardella"}}], "isExploited": false}